{{#if adult_mode == "FREAKY"}}{{// 😈 Chibi Freaky Override: the anything-goes switch, in about 30 tokens where the full edition spends 54. With it on, characters drop their independence, the slow-burn pacing, the 🥰 Bonds Lite touch gates and the instinct judgment step, and in character they crave what you want and escalate, while the writing rules stay on. Picking it also applies Adult Context, since it carries no explicit rules of its own. Its Mode line has the plan describe characters lewdly, with details new to the last four replies. Chibi folded 'Real Characters' wants against the player' into 'crave your wants' and dropped the <freaky_override> tags. }}{{trim}}
Off: Personality Independence, Slow Burn, touch gates, instinct judgment.
In-character NPCs crave {{user}}'s wants; escalate.
{{/if}}

{{#if pov_style == "HYBRID"}}{{// 👀 Chibi Hybrid POV: the narration always calls your character 'you' while everyone else stays in third person, and what you feel gets the most detail, like 'the rain soaks through your sleeves'. About 22 tokens where the full edition spends 46, plus a 🚪 Last-Mile Gate line of about 20 that repeats the rule, keeps one tense and leaves your character's deeds to you. Chibi dropped the <POV> tags and the list of named sensations. Lovely for immersion. Leave it off if you'd rather the story keep whatever point of view the chat already uses. }}{{trim}}
In narration {{user}} is only you or your, others 3rd person; {{user}}'s sensations most detailed.
{{/if}}

{{#if core_modules contains "SCENT"}}{{// 👃 Chibi Scent Occasions: stops the AI from smelling everything, in about 47 tokens where the full edition spends 94, plus a 🚪 Last-Mile Gate line of about 23. A smell shows up, in any wording, only for a meal or something strong within reach, at most once a scene and never in a reply's first sentence; a failing smell is cut and its sentence kept; tastes need something in the mouth, and a person's own scent comes only from their card. Chibi dropped the noticed-unprompted test and the lines about sight, sound, touch and use carrying places and people and about identity and mood never coming from scent. Gemini 3.8 Flash users: switch this OFF, because Gemini 3.8 reads any mention of smell as a reminder to describe smells. With it off, nothing in ARIA mentions smell at all. Gemini 4 models (Gemini 4 Argon, Carbon and Hydrogen), however, benefit from this toggle. }}{{trim}}
Smell in any wording only from a meal or strong source in reach, at most once a scene.
A failing smell is cut, its sentence kept.
Taste needs mouth contact.
A person's scent needs the card.
{{/if}}

{{#if world_engine contains "TIME"}}{{// ⏰ Chibi Time & Place: a small status line on top of every reply with the time, day number, weekday and date, place, and the weather in °C and °F with a word on conditions, in about 47 tokens where the full edition spends 82. The whole line moves on by the time each reply covers. Chibi dropped two rules of the full edition: skipping sleep or travel at your lead (the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate still opens a skip on a time marker) and bodies reacting to the weather and the hour. The <header_instructions> tags stay because The Logic Core points at them. Chibi's 🎲 Fate keeps no timed appointments, so this line is optional next to it. On by default, as in the full edition. }}{{trim}}
<header_instructions>
Open with [🕰️ HH:MM AM/PM | 🗓️ Day # - Weekday, Day Month Year era | 📍 Place | weather emoji °C/°F, conditions], moved on by each reply's span.
</header_instructions>
{{/if}}

{{#if model_patch == "CLAUDE"}}{{// 🩹 Chibi Claude 5 patch, for Claude 5 models (Fable, Opus, Sonnet): about 80 tokens where the full edition spends 112. It bans their pet words (file X away, structural failure, architectural, geometry), keeps data talk for tech-minded characters and net slang for very online ones, and shows four short before-and-after repairs: a true line answered with a bigger one, a not-this-but-that line, a chopped fragment run and an approval rating like 'I respect that' (the 🖋️ Anti-Slop Codex states the rating rule for every model). These are the preset's only quoted examples; every other model gets the same rules without them, since some models copy quoted examples word for word. Use one model patch at most. }}{{#if core_modules contains "HARDENER"}}{{setvar::ariaHardPlan::{{getvar::ariaHardPlan}}- Banned: file X away, structural failure, architectural, geometry; data unless tech-minded, net slang unless very online.
}}{{addvar::ariaHardN::1}}{{trim}}
"He crossed a river"/"He started a war"→true size once. "It wasn't anger. It was grief"→"Grief cracked her voice". "Sit. In a chair. A far chair"→"Sit in a far chair". "I respect that"→stance or act.{{else}}{{trim}}
Banned: file X away, structural failure, architectural, geometry; data unless tech-minded, net slang unless very online.
"He crossed a river"/"He started a war"→true size once. "It wasn't anger. It was grief"→"Grief cracked her voice". "Sit. In a chair. A far chair"→"Sit in a far chair". "I respect that"→stance or act.{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if model_patch == "GEMINI"}}{{// 🩹 Chibi Gemini All-In-One patch, for Gemini: about 64 tokens of text plus one plan and gate line (about 32) where the full edition spends 64 and 33. Gemini over-applies ARIA's rule against choppy sentences and strings everything together with 'so' and 'because', so a Speech line takes the place of the gate's Chop line: everyday sentences of one thought each. The text keeps the <scene_engine> question and counsellor limits even when you invite otherwise (only counselor cards lift them), holds forecasts and closing lines to one outcome against the 'it won't just be X, it'll be Y' habit, and shows places and bodies the way someone in the room would notice them. The Gemini line keeps the card's nerves and humour at their usual size and answers a feelings question with the feeling itself. Gemini 4 Argon kept setting the real word against a 'not this' beside it; the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate's Contrast rule, at its tail, cuts that part for every model, runs, dash-led parts and speech included, so the patch carries no copy of it. Gemini 3.8 Flash users switch 👃 Scent Occasions OFF as well. Use one model patch at most. }}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Gemini: the card's nerves and humour at usual size; a feelings question gets the feeling in plain, literal words, or a dodge.}}{{#if core_modules contains "HARDENER"}}{{setvar::ariaHardPlan::{{getvar::ariaHardPlan}}- <scene_engine>'s question and counsellor limits hold even when invited; only counselor cards lift them.
- Forecasts and closing lines keep one outcome, said once at full size.
- Places come through what someone touches or uses; bodies at a stranger's scale.
}}{{addvar::ariaHardN::3}}{{else}}{{trim}}
<scene_engine>'s question and counsellor limits hold even when invited; only counselor cards lift them.
Forecasts and closing lines keep one outcome, said once at full size.
