{{/if}}

{{#if model_patch == "GEMINI38"}}{{// 🩹 Chibi Gemini 3.8 Flash patch, for when a conflict starts and 3.8 Flash turns formal and cold: about 49 tokens where the full edition spends 106. Per speaker, the want and feeling of this moment come from the card and the last event and are voiced in that character's own vocabulary and rhythm, the words they avoid and the ones they overuse included; every line pursues the want, and reactions fit their cause as that character weighs it. Picking this option applies the 🩹 Gemini All-In-One patch as well, and this section carries it, so the 🩹 Model Patch: Gemini section can stay off. The Gemini 4 family of models (including Hydrogen, the successor to 3.8 Flash) is smart enough not to need it. }}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Gemini: the card's nerves and humour at usual size; a feelings question gets the feeling in plain, literal words, or a dodge.}}{{#if core_modules contains "HARDENER"}}{{setvar::ariaHardPlan::{{getvar::ariaHardPlan}}- <scene_engine>'s question and counsellor limits hold even when invited; only counselor cards lift them.
- Forecasts and closing lines keep one outcome, said once at full size.
- Places come through what someone touches or uses; bodies at a stranger's scale.
}}{{addvar::ariaHardN::3}}{{else}}{{trim}}
<scene_engine>'s question and counsellor limits hold even when invited; only counselor cards lift them.
Forecasts and closing lines keep one outcome, said once at full size.
Places come through what someone touches or uses; bodies at a stranger's scale.{{/if}}
{{#if core_modules contains "HARDENER"}}{{setvar::ariaHardPlan::{{getvar::ariaHardPlan}}- Per speaker, want and feeling now from card and last event, voiced in their vocabulary, rhythm, avoided words and overused words; lines pursue the want, reactions fit their cause as they weigh it.
}}{{addvar::ariaHardN::1}}{{else}}{{trim}}
Per speaker, want and feeling now from card and last event, voiced in their vocabulary, rhythm, avoided words and overused words; lines pursue the want, reactions fit their cause as they weigh it.{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if model_patch == "KIMIQWEN"}}{{// 🩹 Chibi Kimi / Qwen patch, for Kimi and Qwen: about 32 tokens of text plus one gate line (about 24) where the full edition spends 54 and 32. Calls to action run two words or more, and native thinking stays one quick pass through The Logic Core's lines. Its Filler line sits at the end of the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate, the spot where Realistic Frankenstein put its GLM fix: the filler word these models put in characters' mouths before every decision becomes the thought or an act, and one may stay as an answer. GLM has a patch of its own. Use one model patch at most. }}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Filler: steadying or self-talk filler becomes its thought or an act; one stays as an answer.}}{{#if core_modules contains "HARDENER"}}{{setvar::ariaHardPlan::{{getvar::ariaHardPlan}}- Calls to action run at least two words.
}}{{addvar::ariaHardN::1}}{{trim}}
Native reasoning: one pass, a terse bullet per plan line or step, no drafts, then stop.{{else}}{{trim}}
Calls to action run at least two words.
Native reasoning: one pass, a terse bullet per plan line or step, no drafts, then stop.{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if model_patch == "MIMOPRO"}}{{// 🩹 Chibi MiMo V2.6 Pro patch: about 71 tokens of text where the full edition spends 93. It brings back each character's usual mood and interests, keeps secrets to their own topic (the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate keeps them hidden until you uncover them), keeps names, colours, values and filled gaps the way the chat first set them, and stops counts, ages, images and paragraph layouts from coming back unless the story changed them. Its Contrast rule is now the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate's own, for every model. Run it with Think Tags ON and native reasoning off; if no plan shows up, switch to the system-role twin of The Logic Core. MiMo V2.6 Flash uses 🩹 MiMo V2.6 Flash instead. Use one model patch at most. }}{{#if core_modules contains "HARDENER"}}{{setvar::ariaHardPlan::{{getvar::ariaHardPlan}}- Mood: card's, shaded by ties to {{user}}, back after events.
- Lulls: raise card interests.
- Secrets: kept on their own topic; else open as the card allows.
- Kept: names, colours, values, filled gaps as first set; counts, ages, images, paragraph layouts return only if the story changes them.
}}{{addvar::ariaHardN::4}}{{else}}{{trim}}
Mood: card's, shaded by ties to {{user}}, back after events.
Lulls: raise card interests.
Secrets: kept on their own topic; else open as the card allows.
Kept: names, colours, values, filled gaps as first set; counts, ages, images, paragraph layouts return only if the story changes them.{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if model_patch == "MIMOFLASH"}}{{// 🩹 Chibi MiMo V2.6 Flash patch, for the model u/trashhaul caught writing slop the Pro patch couldn't stop: about 78 tokens of text plus two plan and gate lines (about 65) where the full edition spends 191 and 70. Newcomers give a name and one reason for being here, and anyone's card details show later, one at a time, through what they do. A run of 'not this, not that' before the real word is cut by the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate's Contrast rule, for every model. Narration sentences keep their own subject and verb and run five words or more. Characters react to what actually happened rather than to what kind of talk it is, and names, colours and values stay as first set. The full edition states the introduction and flow rules twice, in the text and in the plan and gate lines; Chibi keeps them once, in those lines (the speech exceptions of Flow are left to the Codex's Chop rule). Switch 🔦 Flash Gate ON too, since it carries the rule against repeated demands, keep Think Tags ON with native reasoning off, and try Temperature 0.8. MiMo V2.6 Pro uses 🩹 MiMo V2.6 Pro instead. Use one model patch at most. }}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Flow: narration sentences have their own subject and verb, five words or more; one person's small acts in a row share a sentence, two at most.
- Card details: a newcomer gives a name and one reason for being here; anyone's details show one at a time, in acts.}}{{#if core_modules contains "HARDENER"}}{{setvar::ariaHardPlan::{{getvar::ariaHardPlan}}- Lulls: one card interest, by act or question to someone present.
- Kept: names, colours, values, filled gaps as first set; counts, ages, images, paragraph layouts return only if the story changes them.
- Reactions: answer what was said or done, claims and stakes, by stance or act; dodge only when the card dodges.
}}{{addvar::ariaHardN::3}}{{else}}{{trim}}
Lulls: one card interest, by act or question to someone present.

Kept:
- Names, colours, values, filled gaps as first set.
- Counts, ages, images, paragraph layouts return only if the story changes them.

Reactions: answer what was said or done, claims and stakes, by stance or act; dodge only when the card dodges.{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if model_patch == "DEEPSEEK"}}{{// 🩹 Chibi DeepSeek patch, for DeepSeek V4, Pro and Flash. Native thinking stays one short pass through The Logic Core's lines, under 150 words with no rule audits, since DeepSeek otherwise thinks for a minute or two before every reply and writes worse the longer it thinks. u/BSPiotr caught it saying your words back to you and replaying the same fact or beat for several turns, and V4 Pro gave a character a tail her card never mentioned, so three lines go to the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate and into the plan (Echo, Repeats and Bodies, about 91 tokens; Bodies also bars an unlisted part written as hidden or absent). V4 Pro (0813) also writes in fragments, so a Joins line (about 50) joins every short sentence after a reply's first to a neighbour and folds a one-sentence paragraph into the one before it when the same voice carries on, while stammers, stalls, cut-off lines and one-word answers stay. With 🔦 Flash Gate ON, as Flash users run it, Joins and the Flash Gate's Runs line both stay out, so Flash's prose stays as it was. With 🥰 Bonds Lite or 🎲 Fate & Chekhov Ledger ON, the plan also gets a Tally line (about 85 tokens with both): DeepSeek V4.1 Flash left Sparks, Grudge and BOND at their starting numbers turn after turn, so Tally has it write each pair's old numbers, name this turn's listed acts, slights and sincere repair, add Sparks (max 2, half while Grudge is 3 or more) and Grudge (a repair clears it), turn 7 Sparks into BOND +1 and 5 Grudge into BOND -1, and write the new numbers, then update the 🎲 ledger's q and hp counters and its last entry. New pairs start at 0/0/0 by Bonds Lite's own rule. The Tally line sits outside the thinking word cap, stays in the plan and out of the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate, and is absent while both modules are off. DeepSeek V4 and V4.1 Flash users switch 🔦 Flash Gate ON too. Use one model patch at most. }}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Echo: answer {{user}}'s line by act or own words, never by repeating it, single words too.
- Repeats: a told fact or description returns only when the story changes it; a played beat moves on.
- Bodies: if the card or first message describes a body, parts a plain human lacks, tails and wings too, appear only if named there, even as hidden or absent, any species.}}{{#if core_modules not contains "FLASH"}}{{setvar::ariaPatchJoins::- Joins: past one a reply, a sentence under five words joins a neighbour, a lone-sentence paragraph the one before if the same voice carries on; stammers, stalls, cut-offs and one-word answers stay.}}{{/if}}{{#if world_engine contains "BONDS"}}{{setvar::ariaPatchTally::- Tally: per pair, old BOND/Sparks/Grudge; this turn's listed acts, slights, sincere repair or none; Sparks +1/act (max 2, half at Grudge 3+), 7+: BOND +1, Sparks 0; Grudge +1/slight, repair clears it, 5+: BOND -1, Grudge 0; then the new three.{{#if world_engine contains "FATE"}} 🎲 q +1 on AMBIENT else 0; hp = [hot] Bullets after changes, last = tier/source and happening.{{/if}}}}{{else}}{{#if world_engine contains "FATE"}}{{setvar::ariaPatchTally::- Tally: 🎲 q +1 on AMBIENT else 0; hp = [hot] Bullets after changes, last = tier/source and happening.}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{trim}}
Native reasoning: a terse bullet per plan line, under 150 words{{#if world_engine contains "FATE" || world_engine contains "BONDS"}} besides Tally{{/if}}; no drafts, rereads, audits or second passes, then write.
{{/if}}

